---
export const prerender = true;

import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ServiceLayout from '../../components/service/ServiceLayout.astro';
import AnalyticsDash from '../../components/AnalyticsDash.astro';
import { serviceBySlug } from '../../config/services';

const service = serviceBySlug('ga4-tag-manager')!;
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Our GA4 is already set up. Can you review it instead of starting fresh?',
    a: 'Yes. Existing properties are audited first: events, parameters, conversions, filters, consent settings and data quality. If the foundation is sound, we keep it and fix what is not. Rebuilding without a reason wastes history you may still need.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you work inside our Google Tag Manager container?',
    a: 'That is the normal arrangement. We use your account, document every tag, trigger and variable we add, and leave the container in a state your team can understand and maintain.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will this create duplicate data?',
    a: 'Duplicate collection is one of the first things checked. Implementations include validation passes that look for double firing, missing parameters and conflicting tags before anything is declared done.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you build reports for our team?',
    a: 'Yes, reporting views can be part of the scope: explorations, dashboards and plain language guides so the people making decisions can find the answers without asking an analyst every time.',
  },
];
---

<Base title={service.metaTitle} description={service.metaDescription} canonicalPath={service.path}>
  <ServiceLayout
    service={service}
    lede="A measurement plan first, then GA4 and Google Tag Manager configured to match it: events that mean something, tags that fire once, reports your team can actually read."
    artAlt="Concentric glass rings and flowing ribbon curves on a white pedestal with luminous azure threads"
    faqs={faqs}
    visualTone="tone-white"
    problemTitle="Dashboards full of numbers that answer nothing"
    problemLead="Analytics installations grow by accident: tags added over years, events with three naming styles, conversions that fire twice. Reporting then becomes guesswork."
    deliverablesTitle="Implementation deliverables"
    deliverablesLead="Documentation is part of the build, so the setup survives staff changes."
    processTitle="How an implementation runs"
    processVariant="grid2"
    scopeTitle="What analytics implementation includes"
  >
    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <AnalyticsDash />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="problem">
      <p>
        Most analytics problems are not reporting problems. They are collection problems wearing
        a reporting costume. <strong>If the events underneath the chart are wrong, better
        charts only make the wrongness more confident.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Typical starting points look like this: key actions were never defined so nobody agrees
        what a conversion is, a tag was added in a hurry two years ago and still fires on every
        page, parameters carry four different spellings of the same product name, or consent
        state is ignored by half the tags.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>The fix is sequence, not speed:</strong> define what decisions need to be made,
        design the events that inform them, configure GA4 and GTM to match, then validate the
        data before anyone presents it to a board.
      </div>
      <p>
        That sequence is the entire service. The demonstration above is a simulated dashboard
        built from interface elements, not a connection to live Google data.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="deliverables">
      <ul class="deliver-grid">
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Measurement plan</h3>
            <p>Business questions mapped to events, parameters and conversion definitions.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>GA4 configuration</h3>
            <p>Property settings, conversions, custom dimensions, filters and consent alignment.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>GTM container</h3>
            <p>Tags, triggers and variables organised and labelled so maintenance stays sane.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Validation report</h3>
            <p>Testing evidence: what was checked, where, and the result of each check.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">05</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Reporting views</h3>
            <p>Explorations or dashboards shaped around the questions your team asks regularly.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">06</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Handover notes</h3>
            <p>Plain documentation of the setup so it stays maintainable without us.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="extra">
      <section class="section-sm sv-extra" aria-labelledby="sv-dict-title" style={`--accent:${service.accent}; --soft:${service.accentSoft};`}>
        <div class="container-x">
          <header class="extra-head">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="fade">Example artefact</p>
              <h2 class="display-md" id="sv-dict-title" data-reveal>Event dictionary (illustrative)</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="extra-note" data-reveal="fade">
              Every implementation ships with a shared vocabulary, so a conversation about
              &ldquo;conversions&rdquo; means the same thing to marketing, product and finance.
            </p>
          </header>
          <div class="dict-wrap" data-reveal="fade">
            <table class="dict">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Event</th>
                  <th scope="col">Fires when</th>
                  <th scope="col">Key parameters</th>
                  <th scope="col">Used for</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>view_item</code></td>
                  <td>A product or service detail becomes visible</td>
                  <td><code>item_id, currency, value</code></td>
                  <td>Interest by product, funnel top</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>add_to_cart</code></td>
                  <td>An item is added from a detail or listing page</td>
                  <td><code>item_id, quantity, value</code></td>
                  <td>Intent strength, variant comparison</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>begin_checkout</code></td>
                  <td>The checkout flow is entered</td>
                  <td><code>value, coupon, checkout_step</code></td>
                  <td>Funnel measurement, drop-off analysis</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>generate_lead</code></td>
                  <td>A contact or quote form is confirmed</td>
                  <td><code>form_id, service_interest</code></td>
                  <td>Lead quality by source and page</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>select_promotion</code></td>
                  <td>A merchandised slot or offer is chosen</td>
                  <td><code>promotion_id, slot</code></td>
                  <td>Discovery and recommendation testing</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="dict-note" data-reveal="fade">
            Fictional example to show the format. Your dictionary is written against your
            business, your funnel and your platform.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="process">
      <ol class="p-grid2">
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">01</span>
          <h3>Questions before tags</h3>
          <p>We start with the decisions your team needs to make: which channels to fund, which pages to fix, which funnels to repair. Events are designed backwards from those questions.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">02</span>
          <h3>Design the collection</h3>
          <p>Events, parameters, conversions and triggers are written down as a plan you can review before anything is implemented in your accounts.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">03</span>
          <h3>Configure and document</h3>
          <p>GA4 and GTM are configured to the plan, with every addition labelled and explained in the handover notes as we go.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">04</span>
          <h3>Validate in production</h3>
          <p>A structured QA pass: trigger every event, check parameters, confirm consent behaviour and look for duplicates before sign-off.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="scope">
      <ul>
        <li>Includes GA4 and Google Tag Manager setup or remediation, event implementation and validation.</li>
        <li>Includes documentation, training notes and a read-out for the team that will use it.</li>
        <li>Work is performed in your accounts: you keep full ownership of every property and tag.</li>
        <li>Server-side tagging, complex data warehouse pipelines and third-party CRM sync are separate scopes.</li>
        <li>This website's dashboard is a visual demonstration and is not connected to live Google data.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager are trademarks of Google LLC. Mentioning them
        here describes the platforms we work with and implies no endorsement or partnership.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </ServiceLayout>
</Base>

<style>
  .sv-extra {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-paper), var(--color-paper-3));
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 7%, transparent);
  }

  .extra-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .extra-head > div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .extra-note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
    max-width: 26rem;
  }

  .dict-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 10%, transparent);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: #fff;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .dict {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    min-width: 44rem;
    font-size: 0.87rem;
  }

  .dict th {
    text-align: left;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 10%, transparent);
    background: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .dict td {
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 7%, transparent);
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .dict tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .dict code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-azure) 7%, #fff);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-azure) 80%, var(--color-ink));
    padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .dict td:first-child code {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .dict-note {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
  }
</style>
